# telegram.conf.example — template for telegram.conf, the Telegram credentials
# shared by every backup script on this host.
#
# Copy it to telegram.conf in the root of this collection (next to the module
# directories), fill in both values and make it 0600. Each module's global.conf
# points at it via TELEGRAM_CONF; lib/runlib/notify.sh sources it, so it must
# contain nothing but these two assignments.
#
# telegram.conf is gitignored and not synced, like every other *.conf. It lives
# inside the tree on purpose: the other secrets of this collection
# (repo.password, global.conf) are here as well, so one place holds everything
# a host has to protect.
#
# Leave both at "xxx" (or leave TELEGRAM_CONF empty in global.conf) to switch
# notifications off everywhere without a code change.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="xxx"
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID="xxx"
